From: blackhat-7 <44942105+blackhat-7@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 04:25:26 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 22/33] STRATA_WAIT_PF: a layer's waits read the next layer's
 dense weights into the Infinity Cache (opt-in)

Wait B (the PCIe share in staging) gets STRATA_WAIT_PF_BLOCKS (32) more blocks of 256 threads, and the combine's wait
for the CPU rows (STRATA_COMBINE_MAPPED) twice as many of 128.  While the waiting thread spins, they read the next
layer's ~66 MB of dense weights (hyper-connection reads first, the shared expert last); the waiting thread bumps a
device word when its flag is up and they stop within one chunk.  The next layer's reads then hit the 96 MB cache.
Nothing computed changes.  Measured on the installed run config (sd0, same windows, paired median a window): code
-0.60 ms (+3.0%), prose -1.11 ms (+5.2%), edit -1.51 ms (+5.5%); windows bit-identical to stock v0.2.9.
